Here's a complete implementation:

```csharp
// In Program.cs

// Configure max request body size (before builder.Build())
builder.WebHost.ConfigureKestrel(options =>
{
    options.Limits.MaxRequestBodySize = 10 * 1024 * 1024; // 10MB
});

var app = builder.Build();

// Ensure uploads directory exists
var uploadsPath = Path.Combine(app.Environment.ContentRootPath, "uploads");
Directory.CreateDirectory(uploadsPath);

// ... existing middleware including app.UseAntiforgery() ...

app.MapPost("/upload", async (IFormFile file) =>
{
    var allowedTypes = new[] { "image/jpeg", "image/png" };

    if (!allowedTypes.Contains(file.ContentType))
        return Results.BadRequest("Only JPEG and PNG files are allowed.");

    if (file.Length > 10 * 1024 * 1024)
        return Results.BadRequest("File size must not exceed 10MB.");

    var extension = Path.GetExtension(file.FileName).ToLowerInvariant();
    if (extension is not ".jpg" and not ".jpeg" and not ".png")
        return Results.BadRequest("Invalid file extension.");

    var fileName = $"{Guid.NewGuid()}{extension}";
    var filePath = Path.Combine(uploadsPath, fileName);

    await using var stream = new FileStream(filePath, FileMode.Create);
    await file.CopyToAsync(stream);

    return Results.Ok(new { fileName, size = file.Length });
})
.DisableAntiforgery() // Remove this line if you want antiforgery enforced
.DisableRequestSizeLimit(); // Or use .RequestSizeLimit(10 * 1024 * 1024)
```

**Key points:**

- **Kestrel limit** caps the raw request body at 10MB globally.
- **Content-type + extension** are both validated to prevent spoofing.
- **`Guid`-based filenames** avoid path traversal and collisions.
- **`.DisableAntiforgery()`** — since your pipeline has `UseAntiforgery()`, API clients (non-browser) will be blocked unless you disable it on this endpoint. Remove that chain call if uploads come from a form with a valid antiforgery token.
- If behind IIS/reverse proxy, also set the limit in `web.config`:

```xml
<system.webServer>
  <security>
    <requestFiltering>
      <requestLimits maxAllowedContentLength="10485760" />
    </requestFiltering>
  </security>
</system.webServer>
```
